    "note": "Last version Amended 2017-09-05 (two floor votes on it); earlier floor vote was on the Amended 2017-04-24 text, which instead extended the 30-day limit to all firearms, in 27535: \"A person shall not make an application to purchase more than one firearm within any 30-day period.\" That text was struck on 9/05; Secs. 2-5 (26835, 27535, 27540, 27590) are gone. Definitions of \"locked container\", \"trunk\", \"plain view\" in 25140(d) not quoted. Marks in the saved text show only changes made on 9/05."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 25140 (Penal Code): (a) Except as otherwise provided in subdivision (b), a person shall, when leaving a handgun in an unattended vehicle, lock the handgun in the vehicle’s trunk, lock the handgun in a locked container and place the container out of plain view, or lock the handgun in a locked container that is permanently affixed to the vehicle’s interior and not in plain view.\nSection 25140 (Penal Code): (b) A peace officer, when leaving a handgun in an unattended vehicle not equipped with a trunk, may, if unable to otherwise comply with subdivision (a), lock the handgun out of plain view within the center utility console of that motor vehicle with a padlock, keylock, combination lock, or other similar locking device.\nSection 25140 (Penal Code): (c) A violation of subdivision (a) is an infraction punishable by a fine not exceeding one thousand dollars ($1,000)."
}